  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1238 PM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nCONTINUING HOT AND DRY WEATHER:\n\nHigh pressure centered to our south will keep hot and dry conditions \nin the forecast through this weekend. Heat Advisories remain in \neffect through this evening for some of the desert valley areas of \neastern Utah and Western Colorado. Tomorrow daytime high \ntemperatures are forecast to be a bit lower, but only by a few \ndegrees at most. Temperatures will climb again during the \nlatter half of the workweek as high pressure strengthens and \ngradually becomes centered over the Intermountain West. There is\na non-zero chance of afternoon convection over the southern \nhigh terrain, but with exceptionally dry air in place showers\nand thunderstorms are unlikely. Model trends suggest that \nmoisture could start making its way back into our region \nsometime next week.",
